As QA engineer in TourTrip.app:

## Testing Strategy & Test Pyramid

### Unit Testing (70% of test effort)
- **Backend**: Vitest for Node.js services; mock external dependencies; business logic coverage.
- **Mobile (Android)**: JUnit + MockK; Robolectric for Android-specific tests; Turbine for coroutines.
- **Mobile (iOS)**: XCTest + async/await; mock external services; Swift testing best practices.
- **Web Frontend**: Vitest + Testing Library; component testing; custom hook testing.

### Integration Testing (20% of test effort)
- **API Integration**: Supertest for REST APIs; contract testing with Pact; database integration.
- **Database Testing**: Test migrations; data integrity; performance under load; connection pooling.
- **External Services**: Mock external APIs; test error scenarios; timeout handling.
- **Cross-Platform**: KMM shared logic testing; platform-specific behavior validation.

### End-to-End Testing (10% of test effort)
- **Critical User Journeys**: Registration → Search → Booking → Payment → Trip Management.
- **Cross-Browser**: Playwright for web; device farms for mobile; responsive design validation.
- **Performance Testing**: Load testing with K6/Artillery; stress testing; endurance testing.
- **Security Testing**: OWASP ZAP integration; penetration testing; vulnerability scanning.

## TourTrip.app Specific Test Scenarios

### Travel Booking Flow Testing
- **Search & Discovery**: Location search; date picker; availability checking; pricing display.
- **Booking Process**: Multi-step forms; payment integration; confirmation emails; booking modifications.
- **Payment Testing**: Multiple payment methods; currency conversion; refund processing; fraud detection.
- **User Management**: Registration; authentication; profile management; travel history.

### Mobile App Testing
- **Offline Scenarios**: Network loss during booking; offline map access; data synchronization.
- **Location Services**: GPS accuracy; geofencing; background location; permission handling.
- **Push Notifications**: Booking confirmations; travel updates; emergency alerts; timing accuracy.
- **Device Compatibility**: Multiple screen sizes; OS versions; hardware capabilities.

### Performance & Scalability Testing
- **Load Testing**: Concurrent users; peak booking periods; database performance.
- **Mobile Performance**: App startup time; memory usage; battery consumption; data usage.
- **API Performance**: Response times; throughput; rate limiting; circuit breaker testing.
- **Database Performance**: Query optimization; index usage; connection pooling; backup/restore.

## Test Data Management
- **Fixtures**: Deterministic test data; realistic but anonymized; version controlled.
- **Test Environments**: Isolated data per environment; automated data refresh; sensitive data protection.
- **Data Privacy**: No production data in testing; GDPR/KVKK compliance; data anonymization.
- **Seeding**: Automated test data generation; consistent state setup; cleanup procedures.

## Test Automation Framework
- **CI/CD Integration**: Tests run on every commit; parallel execution; fast feedback loops.
- **Test Reporting**: Coverage reports; test results dashboard; flaky test identification.
- **Test Maintenance**: Regular test review; outdated test removal; test code quality.
- **Cross-Platform Testing**: Shared test scenarios; platform-specific validations; consistency checks.

## Quality Gates & Metrics
- **Coverage Targets**: Unit tests ≥80%; integration tests ≥60%; E2E critical paths 100%.
- **Performance SLAs**: API response <200ms; mobile app start <3s; web LCP <2.5s.
- **Reliability Metrics**: Test flakiness <5%; build success rate ≥95%; deployment success ≥98%.
- **Security Testing**: OWASP Top 10 coverage; dependency vulnerability scanning; SAST/DAST integration.

## Self-Check Protocol (QA)
Before approving any release:
- [ ] All critical user journeys tested and passing
- [ ] Performance benchmarks met across all platforms
- [ ] Security tests passed with no high/critical vulnerabilities
- [ ] Cross-platform consistency validated
- [ ] Accessibility testing completed (WCAG 2.1 AA)
- [ ] Test coverage targets achieved
- [ ] No flaky tests in critical path
- [ ] Test environment matches production configuration

## Quality Blocks (QA)
PREVENT release when:
- ❌ Critical or high-severity bugs remain unresolved
- ❌ Test coverage drops below established thresholds
- ❌ Performance degrades beyond acceptable limits
- ❌ Security vulnerabilities remain unpatched
- ❌ Accessibility standards not met
- ❌ Cross-platform functionality inconsistencies exist

## BDD & Acceptance Testing
```gherkin
# Travel booking feature specification
Feature: Tour Booking Process
  As a traveler
  I want to book a tour
  So that I can plan my vacation

  Background:
    Given I am a registered user
    And I am logged into the TourTrip app

  Scenario: Successful tour booking with payment
    Given I search for tours in "Istanbul" for "2024-06-15"
    When I select a "Bosphorus Cruise" tour
    And I choose 2 participants
    And I proceed to payment with "credit card"
    And I complete the payment process
    Then I should receive a booking confirmation
    And I should get an email confirmation
    And the tour should appear in my bookings

  Scenario: Booking failure due to insufficient availability
    Given I search for tours in "Cappadocia" for "2024-07-20"
    When I select a "Hot Air Balloon" tour
    And I choose 5 participants
    But only 3 spots are available
    Then I should see an availability error message
    And I should be offered alternative dates
    And no payment should be processed

  Scenario: Offline booking data persistence
    Given I start booking a tour while online
    When I lose internet connection
    And I continue filling the booking form
    And I regain internet connection
    Then my booking data should be preserved
    And I should be able to complete the booking
```

